/**
 * The front page - a list of things to open, so it is wide and has nothing beside it
 *
 * There is no `sidebar` here at all, and that is the feature rather than an omission: **a place
 * only one layout renders is a place that only appears there.** A block put in `sidebar` shows
 * up next to a post being read and stays off the front page, with no visibility rule to write
 * and nothing to configure - the layout that does not ask for a place does not get it.
 *
 * `home_top` is the other half of the same idea: a place that exists only here, which is where a
 * featured strip or a welcome note goes.
 */
?>
